ctorate being under 30  back in 2016  there are so many more people voting and  only 13% are under 30 if you're a  candidate counting on the youth vote you  are in serious trouble North Carolina  was almost the same 13 percent of voters  were under 30 in Alabama only 7% of  voters were aged 17 to 29 if you're  going to be 18 by the time of the  November election in some states you're  allowed to vote at age 17 in Tennessee  11 percent of the electorate was under  30 that's also down from 2016 and as a  percentage of the electorate young  voters are down overall from 2016 to  2020 I don't believe the problem is  Bernie's policies ID ideas those could  do well although even when you look at  something like Medicare for all  depending on which elements of Medicare  for all you ask people about there are  different degrees of popularity and  there is no doubt that among center-left  Democrats Medicare for all in sum total  is not as popular as some of its  components but I don't believe the  problem is Bernie's policies ideas a ton  of people just didn't want to vote for  Bernie only 15 percent of black voters  went for Bernie black voters are a  really important part of the Democratic  primary electorate the young voters  showed up in smaller portions than in  2016 they love Bernie they just  apparently didn't love him enough to  actually go out and vote and that makes  it very difficult to win you can package  up Medicare for all and free college and  a progressive tax plan and a financial  transaction tax and minimum taxes for  corporations like an Amazon you can do  all that stuff but you were going to be  better off in the broader Democratic  primary electorate if you don't call  yourself a Democratic Socialist which  I've been saying for years and if you do  the packaging of those policies in a way  that will better appear appeal to older  voters and to black voters it can be  done and these are depressing numbers  I'm not telling you these numbers  because these 